# nab-index

Fetch package listings and metadata from Python package indexes. This
package implements the PyPI
Simple API and caches responses on disk for [`nab-project`]
and [`nab`].

It provides:

- An asynchronous HTTP interface with `urllib3` by default and optional
`httpx` and `httpx2`
  backends.
- A Simple-API client with JSON and HTML decoders.
- A disk cache for project listings and file metadata responses.
- A multi-index router (ordered named indexes plus per-package overrides
that pin a package to one
  index).
- A small VCS clone helper used by the higher-level VCS policy.

## When to use it

Use `nab-index` if you need a typed PyPI Simple-API client with an on-disk
cache. Most users want
[`nab`] instead.

The API is currently under rapid experimentation, if you use it pin to an
exact version.


